      "message": "No strong suggestions, as I\u0027ve not looked in detail.\n\nPossibly for the function definitions, you could do something like\n```\n- void funcname(int arg1)\n+ void __funcname(int arg1, bool sync)\n...\n+ void funcname(int arg1)\n+ {\n+     __funcname(arg1, false);\n+ }\n```\nTo preserve the function signature\n\nThen you only need to change the ones that are always true to use the new `__funcname(arg1, true)` call. \n\nI\u0027m a little confused around the `fuse_iqueue_ops` changes as well as the virtio_fs() changes as it adds the sync argument but then doesn\u0027t do anything with it. So maybe you can avoid making those changes?  But again I\u0027m not sure I fully understand the change.",
